## Why This Is Asked

Tests offline-first, multi-region flows with eventual consistency and idempotency, a common real-world pain point in global apps.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end coverage across regions
- Deterministic mocks for external services
- Data isolation per tenant
- Idempotent submissions and reconciliation after outages
- CI-friendly parallelization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Playwright test skeleton
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('offline-first order flow', async ({ page }) => {
  await login(page);
  await seedInventory(page, 'RegionA', {sku:'ABC', stock:5});
  await gotoCart(page);
  // Simulate offline
  await page.context().setOffline(true);
  await addToCart(page, 'ABC');
  await page.context().setOffline(false);
  await placeOrder(page);
  await expect(getPaymentStatus()).toBe('COMPLETED');
  // Additional checks omitted for brevity
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you structure mocks to ensure cross-region determinism across CI runs?
- What metrics and retries would you implement to detect and mitigate flakiness?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests spanning multi-tenant boundaries and asynchronous export flows surface data isolation and resilience issues. This question probes end-to-end coverage for real-world SaaS data export use cases like Airbnb and Microsoft enterprise products.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant data isolation across services
- Async background jobs and eventual consistency
- End-to-end validation of blob storage and email delivery
- Idempotent retries and fault injection
- Test data strategy and environment isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example test outline (Playwright + API stubs)
test('tenant-scoped data export end-to-end', async ({ page, api, storage }) => {
  await loginAsAdmin(page);
  await page.click('#start-export');
  await page.waitForResponse(r => r.url.includes('/exports/').and(r.status() === 200));
  const status = await api.get(`/exports/${tenantId}/status`);
  expect(status).toHaveProperty('state', 'COMPLETED');
  const blob = await storage.getBlob(`exports/${tenantId}/data.json`);
  expect(blob).toContain(`"tenantId":"${tenantId}"`);
  // idempotence
  await page.click('#start-export');
  const status2 = await api.get(`/exports/${tenantId}/status`);
  expect(status2).toHaveProperty('state', 'COMPLETED');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you parameterize test data for tenants with different data shapes?
- How would you enforce data privacy in the test environment while validating exports?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for data-import flows are common in cloud applications. This question evaluates practical E2E thinking at a beginner level, covering end-to-end flow, UI feedback, and data integrity.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end flow of uploading data and handling background processing
- Mocking backend services (job queue) for deterministic, reliable tests
- Data seeding to ensure predictable idempotent behavior
- Verifying UI progress indicators and downloadable summary reports

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Playwright snippet illustrating route mocking and upload
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test('data import workflow with progress and idempotency', async ({ page }) => {
  // Seed database with existing records for idempotency testing
  await seedTestData();

  // Mock the job queue response
  await page.route('**/api/import', async (route) => {
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 200,
      body: JSON.stringify({ jobId: 'test-job-123', status: 'processing' })
    });
  });

  // Upload CSV fixture
  await page.setInputFiles('input[type="file"]', 'fixtures/test-data-500-rows.csv');

  // Verify live progress updates
  await expect(page.locator('.progress-bar')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('.progress-text')).toContainText('100%');

  // Verify invalid rows are highlighted
  await expect(page.locator('.invalid-row')).toHaveCount(5);

  // Download and verify summary report
  const [download] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.click('.download-summary')
  ]);

  const report = await download.text();
  expect(report).toContain('Total: 500');
  expect(report).toContain('Valid: 495');
  expect(report).toContain('Invalid: 5');

  // Test idempotency - re-upload same file
  await page.setInputFiles('input[type="file"]', 'fixtures/test-data-500-rows.csv');
  await page.waitForSelector('.upload-complete');

  // Verify no duplicates were created
  const recordCount = await getRecordCount();
  expect(recordCount).toBe(500);
});
```

