## Why This Is Asked

Tests in privacy-preserving analytics must guarantee erasure across all data stores, including caches, materialized views, and backups, while maintaining accurate audit trails for compliance.

## Key Concepts
- DSAR data erasure across microservices
- Event sourcing and tombstone propagation
- Soft vs hard deletes and retention windows
- Cross-region replication and data consistency
- Audit logs and backups scrub policy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test outline for DSAR flow
test('DSAR end-to-end erasure', async () => {
  seedTestUser();
  ingestEvents();
  triggerDSAR();
  await expect(dataRemovedFromPrimaryDB()).toBe(true);
  await expect(eventStoreHasDeletion()).toBe(true);
  await expect(cacheInvalidated()).toBe(true);
  await expect(auditLogsContain('DSAR')).toBe(true);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate that backups are scrubbed after the retention window without impacting restore capabilities?
- What observability signals would you add to detect DSAR failures in a multi-region deployment?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests for per-user feature flags are common in SaaS apps. This question checks the ability to seed data, perform API-driven state changes, and verify UI behavior across login and page reloads in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Per-user feature flags and API seed/reset
- End-to-end UI verification of dynamic layouts
- Test isolation and deterministic CI runs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example using Playwright-like syntax (pseudocode)
// seedUser(), setFlag(), login() are helper utilities
test('compact dashboard toggling', async ({ page, request }) => {
  const { userId, email, password } = await seedUser(request);
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', true);
  await login(page, email, password);
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', false);
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-full')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you guard against flaky UI assertions caused by caching?
- How would you extend the test to cover multiple user segments (roles/regions) and parallel execution?

